{
  "registry_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "THE TREATMENT REGISTRY. This file, not the format spec, defines what the",
    "tool can represent. Adding a treatment is a registry entry, not a spec",
    "change: a reader that meets an id it doesn't know draws it neutrally,",
    "leaves it out of costs and lane totals, and says so (V2_PLAN.md 4.1).",
    "",
    "Adding an entry means answering three questions in the same commit:",
    "what category is it, what does it cost per unit, and how does it render.",
    "",
    "category   keeps non-bike treatments out of 'bicycle lane kilometres'.",
    "measure    linear = the geometry IS the quantity; counted = needs a",
    "           `quantity` on the treatment, in `unit`.",
    "geometry   which geometry kinds the treatment may attach to.",
    "cost       planning-grade ranges. per_km for linear, per_unit for counted.",
    "           null means 'not costed yet' - the tool shows no figure rather",
    "           than inventing one. Costs are METRIC: v2 stores metric and",
    "           converts for display. These are exact conversions of the",
    "           documented per-mile figures, so imperial display reproduces",
    "           the familiar round numbers.",
    "stack_rank draw order ONLY, never semantics. A feature draws EVERY",
    "           treatment it has, widest/lowest rank first. Nothing may treat",
    "           treatments[0] as primary - list order is insignificant."
  ],

